<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
    <canvas id="myCanvas" width="400" height="400" style="border:1px solid black;">
        Your browser does not support the canvas element.
    </canvas>

    <script>
        const canvas = document.getElementById('myCanvas');
        const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

        // Rectangle (fill and stroke)
        ctx.fillStyle = 'blue';
        ctx.fillRect(20, 20, 100, 80);

        ctx.strokeStyle = 'red';
        ctx.strokeRect(140, 20, 100, 80);

        // Circle
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.arc(300, 60, 40, 0, 2 * Math.PI);
        ctx.fillStyle = 'green';
        ctx.fill();

        // Line
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.moveTo(20, 150);
        ctx.lineTo(180, 250);
        ctx.lineWidth = 5;
        ctx.strokeStyle = 'purple';
        ctx.stroke();

        // Rounded rectangle
        ctx.beginPath();
        ctx.roundRect(200, 150, 150, 80, 10);
        ctx.fillStyle = 'orange';
        ctx.fill();

        // Helper function for rounded rect (not built-in)
        CanvasRenderingContext2D.prototype.roundRect = function(x, y, w, h, r) {
            this.moveTo(x+r, y);
            this.lineTo(x+w-r, y);
            this.quadraticCurveTo(x+w, y, x+w, y+r);
            this.lineTo(x+w, y+h-r);
            this.quadraticCurveTo(x+w, y+h, x+w-r, y+h);
            this.lineTo(x+r, y+h);
            this.quadraticCurveTo(x, y+h, x, y+h-r);
            this.lineTo(x, y+r);
            this.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x+r, y);
            return this;
        };
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

**Canvas basics:**
- `<canvas>` requires `width`/`height` attributes
- Get 2D context with `getContext('2d')`
- `fillRect(x, y, w, h)`: filled rectangle
- `strokeRect(x, y, w, h)`: outlined rectangle
- `arc(x, y, radius, startAngle, endAngle)`: circle/arc
- `beginPath()`, `moveTo()`, `lineTo()`, `stroke()`: lines
- `fillStyle`/`strokeStyle`: colors
- `lineWidth`: stroke thickness

