```

**Drag and Drop API Essentials:**
- `draggable="true"` makes element draggable
- `ondragstart`: set drag data with `dataTransfer.setData()`
- `ondragover`: call `preventDefault()` to allow drop
- `ondrop`: handle dropped data with `dataTransfer.getData()`
- `dataTransfer` can store text, HTML, URLs, files
- `effectAllowed` / `dropEffect` control cursor feedback

